PARITY (verbatim from the web source):
  • Data via shared state holders: useVehicles, useCharging(useCostForecast), useFormatting,
    useTranslation. NO networking in the view — it binds the CostForecastWidgetSource seam.
  • buildChartData = (historical ++ forecast).slice(-6); each {month, cost, isForecast}.
  • nextCost = forecast[0].cost ?? 0; lastCost = historical[last].cost ?? 0; trendUp = next >= last.
  • Compact (cols<=1): stats only → Next Month + Trend arrow (no chart).
  • Standard (cols>=2): icon+title header + stats (Next Month, Avg $/kWh, Trend ±Δ) + bar chart.
  • isWide = cols>=3. formatCurrency(amt,d)=`${symbol}${fmtNumber(amt,d)}`; symbol '$', precision 2.
  • Icon trendUp→up(amber) / down(emerald). Empty → "No forecast data".
  • i18n keys: widget.costForecast.{title,description,noData,nextMonth,trend,avgPerKwh,costLabel}
    resolve through the P1/S10 facade — zero hardcoded English literals in code.
  Native-idiomatic additions backed by the source's own `isForecast` field (not web drift):
    forecast bars rendered translucent + an Actual/Forecast legend + per-bar VoiceOver values.

